        "# Introduction\n",
        "\n",
        "We use hash-tables a lot in software programming and there has been a strong desire for a more space and run-time efficient representation of a `map` among C++ users. I recently watched Matt Kulukundis' CppCon 2017 talk, [Designing a fast, efficient, cache-friendly hash Table, step by step](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ncHmEUmJZf4). In this blog-post, I would like to explore the implementation details of the abseil library's `flat_hash_map` data-structure. "
